{
  "_notes": [
    "PROJECT EVE ACTIVITY PLANNER.",
    "This system plans believable free-time activity between hard obligations such as sleep, school and work.",
    "It does NOT override a real work shift, medical emergency, arrest, active fight, or other hard event.",
    "The planner is mostly deterministic/rule-based so hundreds of NPCs can live in the town without constant LLM calls.",
    "Traits, needs, money, relationships, time of day, recent activity, weather/world facts and available town locations shape choices.",
    "The planner creates opportunities; HumanEventEngine still decides deeper behavior such as flirt, gossip, steal, argue, help, break up, etc.",
    "NPCs are allowed to do nothing interesting. Staying home, watching TV, leftovers, scrolling a phone, and routine errands are valid life."
  ],
  "planning": {
    "planningHorizonGameHours": 6,
    "replanEveryGameMinutes": 30,
    "minimumActivityDurationMinutes": 20,
    "maximumActivityDurationMinutes": 240,
    "avoidSameOptionalActivityWithinGameHours": 8,
    "allowSpontaneousChange": true,
    "spontaneousChangeBaseChance": 0.08
  },
